-- title:
--   Approximate left units for a positive $b$ inside its own hereditary subalgebra
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a possibly non-unital C$^*$-algebra, ordered by its positive cone. For $h\in A$ write
--   $$\operatorname{Her}(h)=\overline{\{\,h\,x\,h^{*}\ :\ x\in A\,\}}$$
--   for the norm closure of the set of sandwiches $hxh^*$. It is a closed $*$-subalgebra of $A$, and for positive $h$ it is the hereditary C$^*$-subalgebra generated by $h$.
--
--   **Theorem.** Let $b\in A$ be positive and $\delta>0$. Then there is $e\in A$ with
--   $$e\in\operatorname{Her}(b),\qquad e^*=e,\qquad\|e\|\le1,\qquad\|b-e\,b\|<\delta .$$
--
--   So $b$ admits approximate left units chosen inside its own hereditary subalgebra, in the form of self-adjoint contractions. Such an $e$ is used to compress arbitrary elements into $\operatorname{Her}(b)$ via $x\mapsto e\,x\,e$. For instance, this is how one shows that $0\le a\le b$ implies $a\in\operatorname{Her}(b)$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `Her b` is the topological closure of the range of $x\mapsto b\,x\,b^*$. The order on $A$ is any partial order making $A$ a star-ordered ring, which is necessarily the positive-cone order.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/PureInfiniteness/Hereditary.lean#L439-L455

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_IndividualStrongInfiniteness
import Definitions.Def_OAI_Analysis_CStarAlgebra_PureInfiniteness_ClosedIdeal
import Definitions.Def_OAI_Analysis_CStarAlgebra_PureInfiniteness_PositiveFunctional
import Definitions.Def_OAI_Analysis_CStarAlgebra_PureInfiniteness_Representation
import Definitions.Def_OAI_Analysis_CStarAlgebra_PureInfiniteness_Hereditary

open OAI OAI.MainGap
open Filter
open scoped Topology CStarAlgebra ComplexOrder InnerProductSpace
variable {A : Type*} [NonUnitalCStarAlgebra A]
variable [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]

theorem OAI.MainGap.Her_exists_approx_unit {b : A} (hb : 0 ≤ b) {δ : ℝ} (hδ : 0 < δ) :
    ∃ e : A, e ∈ Her b ∧ IsSelfAdjoint e ∧ ‖e‖ ≤ 1 ∧ ‖b - e * b‖ < δ := by sorry
